        "original_id": "b0fcedbf-83f3-5b98-b3c9-b276c4a89b3b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Tom Courtenay, John Mills\n- Films: King Rat, The Loneliness of the Long Distance Runner, Billy Liar, Doctor Zhivago\n- Honors: Knighthood\n\nFacts:\n- Tom Courtenay was born on 25 February 1937 and is an English actor.\n- Tom Courtenay came to prominence in the early 1960s with the films The Loneliness of the Long Distance Runner (1962), Billy Liar (1963), and Doctor Zhivago (1965).\n- Tom Courtenay was among the supporting cast of the film King Rat, which also included John Mills.\n- Tom Courtenay received a knighthood in February 2001 for services to cinema and theatre.",
